# Reference Point — Comparison Section Display (`h2.display` in `.comparison-head`)

When the user says **"reference point"** for the pinned comparison section headline (e.g. "When the jewellery costs lakhs, trust is the product."), match `h2.display` inside `header.comparison-head` in `#comparison`.

## Structure

```html
<header class="comparison-head">
  <p class="eyebrow">The Comparison</p>
  <h2 class="display">When the jewellery costs lakhs,<br>trust is the product.</h2>
  <p class="lead">One app built for browsing. One built for believing.</p>
</header>
```

Pair with brown `.eyebrow` label above and `.lead` subcopy below.

## Visual spec

| Property | Value |
|----------|-------|
| Element | `h2.display` inside `.comparison-head` |
| Font | `var(--serif)` (Instrument Serif) |
| Size | `var(--display)` → `clamp(2.25rem, 4.4vw, 3.5rem)` |
| Weight | `400` |
| Style | **italic** (full line) |
| Color | `var(--ink-deep)` |
| Line-height | `1.15` |
| Margin | `0` |
| Alignment | centered (via `.comparison-head`) |

## Head wrapper

| Property | Value |
|----------|-------|
| Wrapper | `.comparison-head` |
| Layout | column flex, centered, `gap: 1.5rem` |
| Max-width | `52rem` |

## vs other headlines

| Class / element | Use |
|-----------------|-----|
| `h2.display` in `.comparison-head` | Pinned comparison hero — **italic**, `--display`, `var(--ink-deep)` |
| `h2.display` (base) | Page section heads — **regular** (not italic), `--display`, `var(--ink)` |
| `.compare-callout .title` | Scroll callout card — smaller, `clamp(1.35rem, 2.2vw, 1.85rem)` |
| `h4` in `.cert-feature-head` | Main feature canvas — italic, **`32px`** |
| `h3.title` in `.overview-sub-head` | Subsection head — regular, `--title-sm` |

## Hierarchy rule

Comparison display must stay **larger** than `.compare-callout .title`. Do not cap at `32px` — use `var(--display)`.

## Do not

- Remove italic — this is the distinguishing trait vs base `.display`.
- Shrink to `32px` or `--title-sm` — that collapses hierarchy against callout titles.
- Use plain `h2` without `.display` — loses the section display scale.
- Match base `.display` color (`var(--ink)`) — comparison uses `var(--ink-deep)`.
